abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalisation of root-moment rigidity and the forced-factor step
  used in a parity descent for the Lai-Sprang Littlewood series. Includes
  exact-certificate soundness, named coefficient streams, polynomial and
  Laurent-series bridges, and reproducible exact finite-field experiments.
  The all-shift degree cutoff d<N(N-1) has an ordinary proof in the release
  but is not yet an end-to-end Lean theorem. The all-degree auxiliary bound
  and characteristic-two frontier remain unresolved. The mathematical method
  is attributed to Lai and Sprang. First-formalisation priority and independent
  human peer review are not claimed. Development used OpenAI Codex extensively
  under Greg Baker's research direction.
